{"body":"<!--\r\nThank you for your Pull Request. Please provide a description above and review\r\nthe requirements below.\r\n\r\nBug fixes and new features should include tests.\r\n\r\nContributors guide: https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md\r\n\r\nThe contributors guide includes instructions for running rustfmt and building the\r\ndocumentation, which requires special commands beyond `cargo fmt` and `cargo doc`.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\n\r\nBecause Miri didn't have TCP socket support, the tokio tests which relied on `TcpStream`s and `TcpListener`s had to be ignored when being run with Miri. However, over the past months TCP socket support was added to Miri, so these tests no longer need to be ignored when being run with Miri. \r\n\r\nSome tests were using very small buffers or many iterations which caused them to be very slow with Miri. For the tests I considered important I've changed the buffer size/iteration count, the other tests I've annotated with `#[cfg_attr(miri, ignore)]`. \r\n\r\nA few tests using TCP sockets currently don't work with Miri, but there are open issues/PRs for those:\r\n- `readv` can leak memory: https://github.com/rust-lang/miri/pull/5054\r\n- Host I/O events are only processed when entering the scheduler: https://github.com/rust-lang/miri/issues/5047\r\n\r\nI'll open new PRs here once those issues are fixed in Miri and landed in a nightly rust version. ","files":[{"path":".github/workflows/ci.yml","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"tokio-util/tests/udp.rs","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"tokio/src/io/util/mod.rs","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"tokio/src/net/tcp/listener.rs","additions":0,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"tokio/src/net/tcp/socket.rs","additions":0,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"tokio/src/net/tcp/stream.rs","additions":0,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"tokio/sr